[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Traxler Counterattack"]
[Variation "Traxler: 5.Nxf7 Bxf2+ 6.Kf1"]
[ECO "C57"]
[Character "gambit,sharp"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap,hanging-piece"]
[Themes "tempo-gain,piece-activity"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. Ng5 4... Bc5 5. Nxf7 5... Bxf2+ 6. Kf1 { White declines the bishop and keeps the king on f1. This is objectively White's best, and Black must now find new ideas. }
6... Qe7 { Attacks the knight on f7 and brings the queen into the game. [%cal Ge7f7] }
7. Nxh8 (7. Nd6+ 7... Qxd6 8. Kxf2 8... Qc5+ 9. Ke1 9... Qxc4) (7. Ng5 7... Bb6 8. d3 8... d5) (7. Nc3 7... O-O) (7. d4 7... Rf8) 7... d5 { A pawn sacrifice that gains a tempo: it opens the c8 bishop and attacks the bishop on c4. [%cal Gd7d5,Gd5c4] }
8. exd5 (8. Nc3 8... dxc4 9. Kxf2 9... Bg4 10. Qf1 10... O-O-O) (8. Be2 8... Bb6 9. Nc3 9... dxe4 10. Bh5+ 10... Kf8) (8. d3 8... Bg4 9. Qd2 9... Bb6 10. exd5 10... Nd4 11. c3 11... Be2+) (8. Bb5 8... Bb6 9. Nc3 9... Bg4 10. Be2 10... Bxe2 11. Kxe2 11... dxe4) 8... Nd4 { Threatens ...Nxc2 and brings another piece to the attack. White's king is stuck on f1. [%cal Gd4c2] }
9. d6 (9. Nf7 9... Bg4 10. Kxf2 10... Ne4+) (9. Be2 9... Bh4 10. d3 10... Qf8) (9. h3 9... Bg3 10. c3 10... Nf5) 9... Qxd6 { Takes back the pawn. The engine still prefers White, but Black has a lot of activity. }
10. Nf7 (10. c3 10... e4 11. d3 11... e3) (10. d3 10... Bg4 11. Qd2 11... Bh4) 10... Qc5 { The queen escapes the knight and eyes c4 and f2. [%cal Gd6c5] } 11. d3 11... Bg4 { Develops with an attack on the queen. } 12. Qd2 12... Bh4 *
